{
 "rule": "u = fx x/z + cx, v = fy y/z + cy; pixel (i,j) centre at (i+0.5, j+0.5). Back-projection z = depth (or 1/disparity), x = (u-cx) z/fx, y = (v-cy) z/fy. Non-finite or non-positive z is a hole (null). Scaling: fx' = fx w'/w, cx' = cx w'/w, same for y.",
 "contract": "spec/frames-and-units.md \u00a74",
 "tolerance": 1e-12,
